Z||000000||Kasdan||09-10-2001||11:51 AM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">  As many of you already know, i threw a rod.  Knowing this, Itd be just as cheap to get a nower bigger motor as it would be to do a performance 2.8 rebuild.  Is there anything that would bolt up to the tranny/mounts?  or would any motor i choose need new mounts?  help me out, gie me some options<P>------------------<BR>Tyler Morgan<BR>1986 GT Fastback, <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FIERO2.JPG">       <BR>Holley Ram-Air, Power Steering, K&N Filtercharger, Bosch Wires, Bosch Platinum Plugs, Conrad Distribuiter Cap/Rotor, New GT Seats, New Headliner, New Carpet, Ocelet Exhaust, Red Underbody Light Kit (coming soon)<BR>Aim=FieroDriver1986||||reg||1
Z||000001||dgroves||09-10-2001||12:09 PM||||You're probably gonna have to replace crank and pistons anyhow. Why not go back with a 3.1. Thats what I plan to do with my 2.8 that threw a rod. Acording to what I've read on the forum, it will give about a 15 - 20 HP increase at the wheels.||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfixit58||09-10-2001||02:48 PM||||Kas,<P>As mentioned may times before, the 3.4 is probably the most direct bolt-in performance increase you can find that will look like stock. You can probably get a used short block from the bone-yard for less than $500. In addition to this, you'll have to drill new starter holes, have a bolt welded for the fron mount, use a neutral balanced flex-plate or flywheel and buy a gasket set. So, for much less than $1000, you get a motor that should produce about 20% more Hp and Torque the the 2.8.<P>If your really handy, the Caddy 4.1, 4.5, or 4.9 will bolt to your existing tranny. Conversons are said to run arounf $1500 or less and with the 4.9 you can wind up with about 220 Hp and 275 ft-lbs of torque.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Just do a search on the archives for details.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Roy  :D <BR>Just another stock Blue 87 GT   <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fiero_24||09-10-2001||02:58 PM||||I know you do not want a 2.8 rebuild, but I am going to have 180-200hp after all the mods on my 2.8.  With all brand new sensors, alternator, starter, water pump, performance rebuild, performance valve job with bowl work, perf cam, underdrive pulley, bored out intake, headers, free flow exhaust, and more (I do not want to bore you with a long list).  Yes I know I will not get extra HP out of new parts, but it will be reliable.  I am still under $3000 with all these mods ,parts, and labor (I just have to put the asembled motor in myself).  Yes thats a lot of money, and I am still paying for it, but everything will be new except the wiring harness, intake, and a few mounts.  I just would not waste my money with a scrap yard motor if you only want to do this once.  Just some of my thoughts, sory if I seemed to ramble.<P>Craig<P>------------------<BR>  [<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT<p>[This message has been edited by Fiero_24 (edited 09-10-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000004||artherd||09-10-2001||06:54 PM||||get a used 3.4 and have it rebuilt, or get a NEW one  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">    it's the biggest that looks stock.<P><BR>For around uh, $6-7k it looks like so far (heh, yeipes!) you can have a northstar.... <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
